==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{ON.|is}} {{term|dauðr}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|[ˈd̥øyːðʏr]}}

===Adjective===
{{infl|is|adjective}} {{m}}, [[dauð]] {{f}}, [[dautt]] {{n}}

# [[dead]]

====Synonyms====
* (''dead''): [[dáinn]] {{m}}, [[látinn]] {{m}}

====Derived terms====
*[[víndauður]] {{m}} (passed out from drinking)
*[[fyrr skal ég dauður liggja]]
*[[dauður sjór]] {{m}} (a [[sea]] where no fish is caught)

====Usage notes====
* '''dauður''' can sound heartless in modern Icelandic when used for someone the speaker, or the people he is speaking to, knew. When referring to a specific person, use [[dáinn]] instead, unless you are talking about a historical figure long gone or someone you didn't care about.

